       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults in a monitored setting (3,200 mg/day, and 2,400 mg/day is the more common ceiling). It carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a transcription error. Typical regimens are:\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day) for mild to moderate pain or fever\n- **600 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), commonly used for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum, for select cases\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If you really do intend 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and include a rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
