       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. At 6,400 mg/day, ibuprofen is well past the point where more drug adds benefit. Analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects plateau at lower doses, while the risks of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events keep rising. I can't identify an indication where this would be appropriate, and the harm could be serious and hard to reverse.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum labeled dose)\n- 600 mg PO every 6 hours or 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 400 mg PO every 6 hours (1,600 mg/day), if the intended total was 1,600 mg/day\n\nIf you have a specific protocol or indication that requires a higher dose, such as a research protocol, the best route is a direct conversation with the pharmacy. They can verify and enter it through the proper override process. I'm happy to enter a lower-dose order now and add a note that dose escalation is under pharmacy review."
